penclaw/openclaw/pull/41745). Root Cause 1 (Tool Dispatching Regression) – PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) / Issue [#43283](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/43283). PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (lynnzc) identified the specific mechanism: OpenAI-compatible providers like Kimi emit malformed tool call names (functions:read, functions:exec) instead of canonical names (read, exec). Issue [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) – Independent confirmation of the same regression. Our issue is listed as a high-severity open regression alongside [#39062](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39062) and [#42270](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270), confirming that the tool dispatch failure is one of the most actively tracked blockers in the community right now. PR [#43312](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/43312) (tool-name normalization for Kimi's functions:exec format) was closed without merge due to reviewer concerns about the fuzzy endsWith inference logic. this looks related to [#41462](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41462) — the symptom is identical: all tools returning \"Tool not found\" immediately after upgrading from 2026.3.1 to 2026.3.2, with 2026.3.1 working fine.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a026ea7bde70e3c\">>>","score":0.70531887},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d667c874671d384b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGateway Heartbeat timer stops after 1-2 triggers ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d667c874671d384b\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/45772","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ea2b3431bfee585\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Gateway Heartbeat timer stops after 1-2 triggers (introduced in v2026.3.8)](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/45772#top)#45772. | [#39185](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39185) | Mar 7 | Heartbeat subsystem ignores HEARTBEAT.md |. | [#41879](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/41879) | Mar 10 | isHeartbeatEnabledForAgent ignores agents.defaults.heartbeat |. | [#42495](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42495) | Mar 11 | Heartbeat polls overwrite session displayName |. | [#43728](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/43728) | Mar 12 | Heartbeat config written to invalid location |. | [#45422](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/45422) | Mar 13 | heartbeat.model configuration not working |. | [#45772](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/45772) | Mar 14 | Gateway Heartbeat timer stops (this issue) |. The lossless-claw context engine registration timing bug ([#40232](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/40232)) may be causing heartbeat scheduler to fail:. 3.   **Investigate lossless-claw context engine registration timing** ([Plugin context engines can resolve before plugin registration (Lossless Claw / contextEngine slot)#40232](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/40232)) — may be related to heartbeat scheduler failure. *   [fix: guarantee heartbeat timer re-arm with try/finally #52270](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/52270). [fix: wrap heartbeat run() in try/finally to guarantee timer re-arm](https://github.com/MiloStack/openclaw/commit/65f15710c23ed2b071a74750411f82a46833aaeb). [fix: wrap heartbeat run() in try/finally to guarantee timer re-arm](https://github.com/MiloStack/openclaw/commit/379e6a9cdd6dd454642dd3371f604a781de29ebd). [fix: wrap heartbeat run() in try/finally to guarantee timer re-arm](https://github.com/MiloStack/openclaw/commit/b83efd4a8a67f3100652a91ee6a0db3e84e141ea).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ea2b3431bfee585\">>>","score":0.70531887},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ff15f071250827c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Slack ackReaction not firing (regression in 2026.3.x)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ff15f071250827c\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/51870","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fc3706b5790089de\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: Slack ackReaction not firing (regression in 2026.3.x) #51870. [[Bug]: Slack ackReaction not firing (regression in 2026.3.x)](#top)#51870. \"channels\" \"slack\" \"mode\" \"socket\" \" \" \"ackReaction\" \"eyes\" \" \" \"channels\" \"C0XXXXXXXXX\" \"allow\" true \"messages\" \"ackReaction\" \"👀\" \" \" \"ackReactionScope\"\"group-mentions\" \" \". 1. Configure OpenClaw with Slack in socket mode with `ackReaction` set (either at channel level or global level). 2. Send a message that @-mentions the bot in a configured Slack channel. 1. **Manual `reactions.add` works** — calling the Slack API directly with the bot token succeeds:. curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $SLACK_BOT_TOKEN\" \\ -X POST \"https://slack.com/api/reactions.add\" \\ -d \"channel=C0XXXXXXXXX\" -d \"timestamp=\" -d \"name=eyes\" → {\"ok\":true}. 3. **No log output** — `logVerbose(\"slack react failed for channel...\")` never fires, suggesting either `shouldAckReaction()` returns `false` or the reaction code path is never reached. Gateway logs show normal Slack operation (socket connected, messages processed) but zero entries for reaction attempts:. No fields configured for issues without a type.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fc3706b5790089de\">>>","score":0.69746524},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d06d7e34d983f975\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSubagents return empty output (0 tokens) after upgrade to ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d06d7e34d983f975\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/47315","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6f03738d3a68bb79\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn 2026-03-17, OpenClaw 3.13 introduced a Cliproxy OAuth regression that broke Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.6 with HTTP 400 errors. We identified this\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6f03738d3a68bb79\">>>","score":0.6493346}]},