request to create them all as persistent:. As we've discussed previously, I am currently unable to create persistent sub-agents. The Telegram channel plugin has a limitation where mode=\"session\" (which enables persistence) requires thread=true, and this capability is not supported by the plugin in its current configuration. Therefore, I cannot create them persistently as requested. I can only spawn them for one-off tasks (mode=\"run\") or as ACP sessions if an agentId is provided or acp.defaultAgent is configured. Since I cannot create them persistently, I cannot list their names as persistent agents. • Proceed with developing these components myself using web\\_search for research and my own coding capabilities for logic outlines, and then later initiate ACP sessions for the actual code generation if the agentId or configuration issues are resolved. • If you have an agentId available for ACP tasks, I could try spawning them that way, but they might not be persistent.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"187fa7e6f104a367\">>>","score":0.9992505},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"56a78279434771c8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: agent:main:main session responds to Telegram DMs ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"56a78279434771c8\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/40005","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bdfa413c93c88346\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nBoth agent:main:main and agent:main:telegram:direct respond to every Telegram DM. User receives two replies per message. OpenClaw version.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bdfa413c93c88346\">>>","score":0.9987356}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775073890541}}
{"type":"message","id":"d9139e51","parentId":"1fb21af0","timestamp":"2026-04-01T20:04:50.612Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_EOHFukMklMXnVm5nm4SJAe1L|fc_062cdbb2f0b8822d0169cd7a5fc7408191a1f7e94ad4b3a42c","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"Context compaction loop runs indefinitely, burning credits with no output\\\" openclaw discussion\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1528,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ce6d921f651cb05c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAuto-compaction not triggered during tool-use loops, leading to ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ce6d921f651cb05c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24800\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"56715d654974cd7a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhen an agent enters a long tool-use loop (many consecutive tool calls without user messages), the context grows steadily but auto-compaction\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"56715d654974cd7a\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.999892\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7301da504517bba0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGood article on how to optimize your OpenClaw agent so it doesn't ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7301da504517bba0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2024124975545000229\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4217a89f2537a819\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nI Burnt $127 in API Credits Before I Fixed These OpenClaw Mistakes. Everyone on Twitter said OpenClaw would build my startup while I slept.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4217a89f2537a819\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99985576\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"25a9900a4361f166\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nthe tokens got burned by dragging a huge context forward #1594\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"25a9900a4361f166\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/1594\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2acc77916e4a25ee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChange cron behavior so it runs a shell script only and only wakes the agent when there's a finding (or run less frequently). Turn on aggressive\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2acc77916e4a25ee\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99936384\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c8d30fbcab497677\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHow to Optimize OpenClaw: Memory, Concurrency, and Context ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c8d30fbcab497677\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://medium.com/@creativeaininja/how-to-optimize-openclaw-memory-concurrency-and-context-that-actually-works-84690c2de3d7\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f87fc7bc8da0587\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe core solution is called Context Triangulation, and once you understand it, you'll wonder why static loading was ever the default. Instead of\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f87fc7bc8da0587\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99921453\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cea35b273a504a75\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nI've Been Running OpenClaw Wrong — Here's What Actually Fixed It\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cea35b273a504a75\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://medium.com/@orami98/ive-been-running-openclaw-wrong-here-s-what-actually-fixed-it-1afe8d8f30db\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d53cf1a24eb0d5b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# I’ve Been Running OpenClaw Wrong — Here’s What Actually Fixed It. Three weeks ago, I was complaining in a Discord that OpenClaw kept “forgetting” things. That one change fixed 80% of my OpenClaw frustrations overnight. I spent the following two weeks tearing apart my setup, stress-testing different configurations, and rebuilding my OpenClaw stack from scratch. Everything in this article was tested on a live OpenClaw instance running the `2026.3.x` release line, connected via Telegram, and used as my primary daily driver for two full weeks before I wrote a single word here. During this period I ran Sonnet 4.6 as my interactive primary with Opus 4.6 reserved exclusively for overnight cron jobs and heavy coding tasks — a quota-aware configuration I explain in detail in Section 2. I tracked token consumption across model configurations, logged all cron job execution times, and measured context degradation across threaded vs. First, OpenClaw loads your entire conversation history into its context window every time you send a message.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d53cf1a24eb0d5b\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9975656\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"\"Context compaction loop runs indefinitely, burning credits with no output\" openclaw discussion","provider":"tavily","count":5,"tookMs":1528,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ce6d921f651cb05c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAuto-compaction not triggered during tool-use loops, leading to ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ce6d921f651cb05c\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24800","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"56715d654974cd7a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhen an agent enters a long tool-use loop (many consecutive tool calls without user messages), the context grows steadily but auto-compaction\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"56715d654974cd7a\">>>","score":